WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Welcome to Facilitate Education and Enterprise Learning. I’m

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.640
Brian Kennedy Jr. This course is for educators

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.960
and program teams who want learners to leave

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.360
with work they can use. You will define

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.240
a focused pilot, plan a demonstration and practice

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.600
sequence, and assess observable performance through an original

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.240
rubric. We will make room for different access

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.880
needs and for learners who choose private examples

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.000
instead of public sharing, outreach or selling. You

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.400
will also build a minimal evidence plan that

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.960
keeps consent, missing work and the limits of

00:00:31.013 --> 00:00:33.600
a small pilot visible. The result is a

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.800
delivery package and a next-cycle decision, not a

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.560
claim of accreditation or proven long-term impact. Start

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.120
by choosing one primary learner group and one

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.520
artifact they should be able to produce. That

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.240
choice will guide the session, the assessment and

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.360
the evidence you collect.
